Subject: [PATCH] fix(models): preserve cubes without visible faces

Bedrock geometry can contain cubes with an empty UV face map. Omit these
cubes from Java model elements instead of inventing an unresolved texture
face or exporting an invalid element with no faces. Java 26.3 requires at
least one face per element; a wholly invisible model can have no elements.

Keep source bones and cubes available to the native renderer. Reindex
exported group children after filtering, and normalize copied UV arrays so
repeated export does not mutate cached model geometry.

Recorded CubeCraft turret, watermelon and gravestone models contain these
cubes. Synthetic tests cover mixed and wholly invisible geometry, valid
visible texture references, preserved source cubes and repeatable export.
